<h2>How to use the lighting visualizer</h2>
<p class="lead">Landscape lighting is hard to imagine from a list of fixtures. This visualizer lets you build a lighting plan in layers, the same way a designer does, and see how each layer changes the feel of a home.</p>
<ol class="steps">
  <li><strong>Start with a preset.</strong> "Subtle" shows a restrained front-elevation look, "Balanced" is a typical full-property design, and "Path &amp; entry" shows how much a few path lights alone can do.</li>
  <li><strong>Toggle each layer.</strong> Architectural lighting gives the house shape; path lighting makes it safe to arrive; tree lighting adds height and depth; patio lighting extends your living space.</li>
  <li><strong>Slide the color temperature.</strong> Most homes in Spring look their best between 2700K and 3000K. Push toward 4000K and watch brick and wood turn flat and gray.</li>
  <li><strong>Dim it down.</strong> Lower brightness often looks more expensive, not less. Contrast is what makes features stand out.</li>
</ol>
<h2>What the numbers mean</h2>
<p>The fixture count and wattage use typical LED values for each layer (for example about 3 W for a path light and 6–9 W for an uplight). The monthly cost assumes six hours a night at $0.15 per kWh, and the transformer suggestion follows the <a href="/landscape-lighting-transformer-sizing/">80% loading rule</a>. Real designs vary with the property, so treat these as a feel for scale rather than a quote.</p>
<div class="callout"><strong>Designer's tip:</strong> the best night-time views usually come from two or three layers done well, not every layer at full power. Leave some darkness so the lit features have something to stand out against.</div>
<p>When you are ready to see it on your own home, <a href="/quote/">request a free consultation</a> and Spring Landscape Lighting will walk the property, then design the real thing. You can also explore the <a href="/landscape-lighting-techniques/">12 core lighting techniques</a> or browse our <a href="/inspiration/">inspiration gallery</a>.</p>
